cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you discuss or evaluate NVMatrixEngine, cite this software and identify the version, commit and configuration. Citation does not grant reuse rights."
type: software
title: "NVMatrixEngine: Real-Time Game Engine with GPU Fluids and Path-Traced Caustics"
authors:
  - name: "codejeet"
    website: "https://github.com/codejeet"
version: 0.1.2-preview
date-released: "2026-09-17"
repository-code: "https://github.com/codejeet/NVMatrixEngine"
url: "https://github.com/codejeet/NVMatrixEngine/releases/tag/v0.1.2-preview"
abstract: >-
  Native C++20 DirectX 12/DXR game engine coupling GPU APIC/FLIP liquid
  simulation, a staggered MAC pressure grid, anisotropic particle surface
  reconstruction and sparse procedural liquid geometry with camera path tracing,
  spectral photon caustics and DLSS Ray Reconstruction. Optional experiments
  include CUDA interop, narrow-band particle/grid ownership, adaptive optical
  sampling and opaque-primary ReSTIR PT. Includes an interactive Windows Water
  Lab, validation fixtures and implementation notes. Not a general BDPT integrator
  or a fully sparse multiresolution fluid solver; public portfolio source with
  rights reserved.
keywords:
  - game engine
  - GPU fluid simulation
  - real-time liquid simulation
  - APIC
  - FLIP
  - MAC pressure projection
  - procedural ray tracing
  - DirectX 12
  - DXR
  - spectral photon mapping
  - water caustics
  - anisotropic surface reconstruction
  - CUDA interoperability
  - narrow-band FLIP
  - ReSTIR PT
  - DLSS Ray Reconstruction
